CPLEX Parameter File Version 22.1.1.0
# Suggested parameters for plexos2gtopt-derived MIPs (large unit-commitment
# MIPs with a sizeable integer share).
#
# Overrides on top of CPLEX defaults:
#
#   1. CPXPARAM_MIP_Cuts_Gomory = 1
#      Moderate Gomory cut generation.  The aggressive setting (2) can spend
#      long root-cut rounds on degenerate weeks that barely move the bound;
#      combined with the reduced cut passes below the root-cut work is
#      bounded.
#
#   2. CPXPARAM_LPMethod = 4
#      Barrier for the root relaxation of these large cold-start LPs, where
#      simplex variants can stall.
#
# Caveat: forcing barrier here makes warm-started SDDP iteration LPs
# slower (dual simplex is the natural choice on warm bases).  If this same
# prm is loaded under SDDP, comment out the LPMethod line and let the
# solver's auto-pick choose dual on warm bases.
#
#   3. CPXPARAM_MIP_Tolerances_MIPGap = 0.01
#      Stop at a 1 % relative MIP gap; the last fraction of a percent is
#      dispatch-irrelevant for these studies.
#
#   4. CPXPARAM_MIP_Limits_CutPasses = 1
#      CPXPARAM_MIP_Strategy_RINSHeur = 50
#      CPXPARAM_MIP_Strategy_HeuristicEffort = 0.30
#      Capping cut passes, running RINS every 50 nodes, and raising
#      heuristic effort (default 0.05) aim to find a good incumbent early so
#      the gap closes fast.  One cut pass (not zero) is kept so cuts and
#      heuristics can still escape poor incumbents.  Pure search-strategy
#      params — NO LP coefficient or scaling change ⇒ LMPs, water values
#      and reduced costs are unaffected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CPXPARAM_MIP_Cuts_Gomory                        1
CPXPARAM_LPMethod                               4
CPXPARAM_MIP_Tolerances_MIPGap                  0.01
CPXPARAM_MIP_Limits_CutPasses                   1
CPXPARAM_MIP_Strategy_RINSHeur                  50
CPXPARAM_MIP_Strategy_HeuristicEffort           0.30
